{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Historical counterexample audit complete. Corpus: 574 closed tickets with a signed plan-review attestation and an Acceptance Criteria match. Counts below are blast-radius indicators, not claimed FP rates: 498/574 lack a literal `## Approach`; 223/574 lack literal `## Scope`; 103/574 have empty structured file_impact. Of 573 signed/closed tickets with parsed AC checkboxes, a strict proof-lexicon detector would reject 493 and the current-style conjunction/comma compound heuristic hits 401. Of 33 signed/closed tickets with a literal Testing section, 5 contain no failure/edge/empty/invalid/timeout/boundary/malformed marker.\n\n1. Required nonempty canonical sections — DISPROVED AS WRITTEN; NARROW TO SEMANTIC CONTENT/ALIASES. Ticket 003d-e6b0-9e58-4b52 (`adamantine-claimable-equine`) is closed with both plan-review PASS and completion-verifier PASS. It has `## Why`, `## What`, `## Scope`, and AC, but no `## Approach`. Its What section is fully executable: “Replace each with a test that provokes the real behavior…” A literal Approach requirement would reject a valid plan whose mechanism is carried by the historical What vocabulary. Accept semantic aliases and non-heading compact plans; headings are a coaching convention, not a sound hard oracle.\n\n2. Placeholder-free exact lexicon — PHRASE-ONLY FAILURE IS DISPROVED; ADVISORY-ONLY/NARROW. Ticket 03c6-44ef-e420-4e31 (`clueless-anguished-harpyeagle`) is closed with plan-review PASS and completion-verifier PASS. Its executable checklist says: “Update infra/gerrit/setup-project.sh / smoke-check if they reference the removed label/ACL.” A `check if` matcher flags this, but it is not a deferred design choice: the condition is mechanically decidable and the action is fully specified. The ticket later records the live cutover and operator evidence. No signed/closed ticket was found with the exact lexicon inside a literal Approach/Scope section, so the narrowly scoped detector has no direct corpus disproof; however many valid plans, including this one, express scope in AC rather than a Scope heading. A semantic section normalizer would expose this false positive. Treat the lexicon as a hint; distinguish unresolved choice from bounded conditional work.\n\n3. Per-AC explicit proof coverage — DISPROVED AS A HARD RULE; ADVISORY-ONLY. Ticket 003d has five ACs and zero `verified by`/`verify with` markers. Examples: “Each error class is raised by exercising the failing path” and “fs_tools reuse is proven by identity, not existence.” These are precise behavioral oracles even without a proving-clause sentinel; plan-review and completion-verifier both passed. A strict marker detector would reject it. Recognize behavioral assertion forms, and expose proof coverage as coaching rather than verdict.\n\n4. Grounded edit-set requiring Scope + file_impact — DISPROVED UNCONDITIONALLY; NARROW APPLICABILITY. Ticket 0730-6ceb-88c3-430c (`enervated-snoozy-needletail`) is a valid analysis/probe ticket, closed with plan-review PASS and completion-verifier PASS, with empty file_impact. Its plan explicitly says the probe is a local uncommitted workpad and the durable output is ticket comments. Completion comments record 34 live pairs, 541 scored findings, decision-rule results, and follow-up provenance. Requiring an edit-set would invent nonexistent repository edits. Exempt read-only analysis, operational, and external-attestation work when an explicit no-edit/output contract is present.\n\n5. AC conjunction/vague/hedge hygiene — DISPROVED AS A FAILURE ORACLE; ADVISORY-ONLY. Ticket 090f-4f7c-44ba-49ae (`wait-solar-haste`) is closed with both attestations. Its final AC says tests cover `show` AND `verify_signature` for stamped and pre-stamp attestations, including schema/model validation. Multiple conjunctions describe one coherent cross-surface compatibility matrix; splitting it would obscure the invariant and duplicate setup. Deterministic conjunction counts cannot distinguish bundled independent deliverables from one atomic matrix. Keep only as a review prompt.\n\n6. Testing section must name happy + negative scenario — DISPROVED; REJECT HEADING-TRIGGERED APPLICABILITY. Ticket 35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5 (`finicky-rainbowy-weevil`) is closed with both attestations. Its Testing section contains regression/invariant checks: gate-rubric consistency, targeted pytest, an epic AC+Context pass case, and an exact score assertion. It has no failure/edge/empty/invalid/timeout/boundary marker because the work is a mechanical heading/weight migration; a negative user-flow taxonomy is inapplicable. Require negative scenarios only after semantic applicability establishes new user-facing behavior, not merely because a Testing heading exists.\n\nNet recommendation: none of the six should directly fail clarity in their original form. Section presence and edit-set can become reliable after explicit applicability/alias rules. Placeholder, per-AC proof, conjunction hygiene, and testing-shape remain deterministic signals suitable for evidence-bearing advisory output, but history disproves using them as hard validity criteria."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785190454306027001,"uuid":"bae6f997-d1fe-4362-9e21-a813f010ece4"}